{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "German -> English food-name aliases, applied at query time by the FDC backend only.",
    "why": "openplate ships en + de, and USDA FoodData Central is English-only. Without this table every German item name fails retrieval and resolves to null macros. The LCC backend needs none of this - it is multilingual and takes a locale natively.",
    "authorship": "Hand-authored for openplate-inference (2026-08-13). Ordinary bilingual vocabulary, no third-party dataset, no licence attached to it, deliberately so - see data/fdc-foods.json's _meta for the licence posture this repo has to keep clean.",
    "coverage": "The ~180 foods that actually show up on a photographed plate in German-speaking markets, plus the cooking-form words that decide which USDA row is right. It is not a dictionary and does not try to be: an unmatched German name simply falls through to the untranslated query and, failing that, to null macros.",
    "mapping": "Left side is normalized (lower case, umlauts as typed). Both the whole-string form and the per-token form are tried - 'gebratene haehnchenbrust' resolves token-wise even though only 'haehnchenbrust' has an entry.",
    "umlauts": "Each umlaut entry is duplicated in its transliterated form (haehnchenbrust as well as hahnchenbrust) because a vision model's transcription of a German word is not reliably accented."
  },
